So, you'll have to try and figure out your own methods for defeating the monsters.

35
00:02:35,420 --> 00:02:40,100
Still, all things considered, the game's creators were actually pretty smart.

36
00:02:41,060 --> 00:02:45,500
It's programmed so that the player is guaranteed to get stronger as they progress.

37
00:02:46,700 --> 00:02:51,400
And most likely, it's all for the purpose of making that child stronger.

38
00:02:51,400 --> 00:03:06,740
One must battle a wide variety of enemies in Nen combat.

39
00:03:06,740 --> 00:03:12,280
The most critical of all the battle skills is the ability to think quickly.

40
00:03:13,420 --> 00:03:18,640
You have to get used to thinking constantly until your thoughts are tied to your reflexes.

41
00:03:19,160 --> 00:03:22,560
This game is a training regimen to help you achieve that.

42
00:03:22,560 --> 00:03:28,300
The hardest monster to defeat in this area is the Bubble Horse.

43
00:03:28,840 --> 00:03:32,020
Once they clear that, they'll have completed the second phase.

44
00:03:40,440 --> 00:03:41,060
That's who!

45
00:03:41,060 --> 00:03:58,000
When it comes to analysis and physical strength, Killua has the edge.

46
00:03:58,440 --> 00:04:02,900
But Gon makes up for it with his concentration and lightning-fast recovery speed.

47
00:04:02,900 --> 00:04:06,580
Those two really make a perfect team.

48
00:04:08,580 --> 00:04:11,660
Okay, now we'll begin training you in defense.

49
00:04:19,180 --> 00:04:20,540
Hey, is that...

50
00:04:20,540 --> 00:04:21,500
That's right, Gon.

51
00:04:21,760 --> 00:04:24,120
This is the technique you've both been using.

52
00:04:24,660 --> 00:04:30,820
Ten, Zetsu, Ren, Hatsu, and Gyo are all combined in this single technique.

53
00:04:31,380 --> 00:04:31,980
Called Ko!

54
00:04:32,900 --> 00:04:37,620
You focus every ounce of your aura into one part of your body and then attack.

55
00:04:37,980 --> 00:04:42,100
This method gives it far greater power than your regular attacks ever could.

56
00:04:43,100 --> 00:04:45,480
I'm going to attack you with my fist.

57
00:04:45,760 --> 00:04:48,680
And you must block my attacks by any means necessary.

58
00:04:48,960 --> 00:04:50,200
No dodging allowed.

59
00:04:51,680 --> 00:04:52,940
Figured it out yet?

60
00:04:53,420 --> 00:04:54,200
That's right.

61
00:04:55,640 --> 00:04:59,940
If you use your aura to block normally, you'll take considerable damage.

62
00:05:00,940 --> 00:05:01,940
So instead...

63
00:05:01,940 --> 00:05:04,280
We should use Ko as well.

64
00:05:04,560 --> 00:05:05,620
You're half right.

65
00:05:07,020 --> 00:05:08,680
Ko versus Ko.

66
00:05:09,100 --> 00:05:14,040
Unless the disparity in power is too great, a well-executed block will protect you.

67
00:05:14,040 --> 00:05:22,520
But if your opponent hits you in a place where you weren't using Ko, you'll be destroyed.

68
00:05:22,520 --> 00:05:25,980
Then we should use Ko on our entire body.

69
00:05:25,980 --> 00:05:27,700
But it sounds contradictory.

70
00:05:27,700 --> 00:05:28,880
Exactly.

71
00:05:28,880 --> 00:05:31,720
This technique combines both Ten and Ren.

72
00:05:31,720 --> 00:05:33,040
It's known as Ken.

73
00:05:34,380 --> 00:05:38,820
You defend yourself by shrouding your body in much more aura than usual.

74
00:05:39,460 --> 00:05:43,640
It isn't as strong as Ko, of course, but it's infinitely more practical.

75
00:05:44,920 --> 00:05:46,940
Gon, use Ren, please.

76
00:05:48,860 --> 00:05:51,580
Ken is sustaining that for a long time.

77
00:05:51,580 --> 00:05:55,200
Now protect yourself from my punch, if you can.

78
00:05:55,200 --> 00:06:02,160
It's so slow.

79
00:06:02,160 --> 00:06:16,940
You let your guard down when you saw how slowly I was moving.

80
00:06:16,940 --> 00:06:20,660
If you'd stopped using Ken, I would have crushed your face.

81
00:06:21,360 --> 00:06:23,500
That's the power of Ko by itself.

82
00:06:23,900 --> 00:06:27,900
When I add the speed and power packed into a normal punch, it gets stronger.

83
00:06:28,100 --> 00:06:30,140
Many times stronger as a matter of fact.

84
00:06:30,520 --> 00:06:31,940
Perhaps even dozens.

85
00:06:31,940 --> 00:06:36,620
I'll start by going slowly.

86
00:06:36,620 --> 00:06:38,620
And don't expect a warning.

87
00:06:40,080 --> 00:06:43,680
Keep using Ken and try your best to withstand my attacks.

88
00:07:01,940 --> 00:07:06,360
That was almost a full two minutes.

89
00:07:06,800 --> 00:07:11,580
I had no idea that trying to maintain my Ren for so long would be so hard.

90
00:07:12,080 --> 00:07:17,540
If you want to stand a chance, you'll need to be able to sustain Ken for at least 30 minutes.

91
00:07:22,500 --> 00:07:24,300
Alright, we're done.

92
00:07:24,560 --> 00:07:25,920
Time to practice Ken.

93
00:07:31,940 --> 00:07:39,000
Good. That's 30 minutes.

94
00:07:39,420 --> 00:07:42,240
You've certainly gotten a lot tougher over the past month.

95
00:07:42,540 --> 00:07:43,400
The number three!

96
00:07:44,080 --> 00:07:44,440
Ding!

97
00:07:44,980 --> 00:07:46,100
Kilowa by a hair.

98
00:07:46,840 --> 00:07:48,680
Gon, give me a thousand push-ups.

99
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:52,040
Alright.

100
00:07:52,460 --> 00:07:54,660
Today, we'll begin actual combat training.

101
00:07:55,740 --> 00:07:56,300
Ken!

102
00:07:56,300 --> 00:08:09,500
In your current state, both your attack power and your defense are at 50, which means that at this point, if you were to fight each other using Ken, you wouldn't be able to cause much damage at all.

103
00:08:10,000 --> 00:08:10,820
So what do you do?

104
00:08:11,180 --> 00:08:12,200
