108
00:08:17,040 --> 00:08:18,060
We use Gyo.

109
00:08:18,400 --> 00:08:18,840
Correct!

110
00:08:18,840 --> 00:08:29,720
So with an even split, right at the moment of attack, shift offensive and defensive power of your right fist to 70, and the rest of it to 30.

111
00:08:30,500 --> 00:08:35,240
And then, you can use Gyo to change the ratio of power to suit your situation.

112
00:08:35,820 --> 00:08:36,900
This is called Ryu.

113
00:08:37,980 --> 00:08:42,820
Now set your right hand to 70 for offense and defense, and the rest to 30.

114
00:08:43,500 --> 00:08:45,000
It doesn't have to be precise.

115
00:08:45,180 --> 00:08:45,960
Just try it out.

116
00:08:45,960 --> 00:08:51,860
Left foot to 80, your body to 20.

117
00:08:53,040 --> 00:08:55,700
Now head to 60, your body to 40.

118
00:08:58,280 --> 00:09:03,140
Do this for 30 minutes three times a day, along with your current training regimen.

119
00:09:03,620 --> 00:09:07,160
Also, we'll begin sparring.

120
00:09:07,780 --> 00:09:10,000
Use Ryu just as I taught you.

121
00:09:10,360 --> 00:09:11,980
Start out by trying it slowly.

122
00:09:11,980 --> 00:09:18,680
When you're on the defensive, you'll want to determine your opponent's attack power before defending with Ryu.

123
00:09:19,880 --> 00:09:21,860
With that said, begin!

124
00:09:22,420 --> 00:09:23,960
I'll go first, okay, Gon?

125
00:09:25,520 --> 00:09:28,620
Right foot, 55 on both fronts.

126
00:09:29,160 --> 00:09:31,740
Right foot, 60 offensive and defensive.

127
00:09:32,440 --> 00:09:33,020
