If the stone in your hand breaks, it's over.

165
00:11:49,220 --> 00:11:49,900
Dammit!

166
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:51,360
I messed it up!

167
00:11:51,740 --> 00:11:53,240
What are you talking about?

168
00:11:53,360 --> 00:11:54,840
You were actually doing well.

169
00:11:54,840 --> 00:11:59,080
Okay, let's do a transmuter exercise next.

170
00:11:59,300 --> 00:12:00,240
Now, now.

171
00:12:00,420 --> 00:12:01,740
Don't be so hasty.

172
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,920
You're only allowed to train in one category per day.

173
00:12:05,500 --> 00:12:06,160
A six!

174
00:12:06,660 --> 00:12:07,040
Right!

175
00:12:07,400 --> 00:12:08,000
Tie it again.

176
00:12:09,060 --> 00:12:09,620
Really?

177
00:12:10,180 --> 00:12:11,260
We keep tying.

178
00:12:11,680 --> 00:12:15,460
All that means is that you're both growing a lot more accustomed to using Gyo.

179
00:12:15,460 --> 00:12:18,200
But it's not any fun if there's no winner.

180
00:12:18,520 --> 00:12:20,740
Then let's decide with rock, paper, scissors.

181
00:12:21,400 --> 00:12:24,060
And the loser has to do a thousand push-ups, okay?

182
00:12:24,380 --> 00:12:25,300
Fine by me.

183
00:12:25,660 --> 00:12:26,980
Now show me rock!

184
00:12:27,440 --> 00:12:28,600
John can bone!

185
00:12:28,980 --> 00:12:30,380
John can bone!

186
00:12:30,820 --> 00:12:31,720
I win!

187
00:12:32,560 --> 00:12:33,480
Dammit!

188
00:12:33,480 --> 00:12:34,300
Hey, boys.

189
00:12:34,600 --> 00:12:37,460
Have you heard that this game is based on the martial arts?

190
00:12:37,460 --> 00:12:45,060
Paper represents a palm attack to the organs.

191
00:12:45,560 --> 00:12:48,000
Scissors represent a finger jab to the vitals.

192
00:12:48,700 --> 00:12:51,600
Rock represents a punch targeting muscle and bone.

193
00:12:52,600 --> 00:12:57,220
A long time ago, martial arts were called jokin or evil fist

194
00:12:57,220 --> 00:13:00,780
and considered so destructive that they were completely forbidden.

195
00:13:01,220 --> 00:13:05,200
But masters were able to continue their training by pretending to play.

196
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:10,460
And that's how many people think jokin or rock, paper, scissors first came to be.

197
00:13:10,760 --> 00:13:11,480
Wow.

198
00:13:11,940 --> 00:13:13,120
You're really old.

199
00:13:15,020 --> 00:13:15,900
That's it!

200
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:16,540
The jokin!

201
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:17,640
Huh?

202
00:13:19,840 --> 00:13:21,000
Evil fist!

203
00:13:25,620 --> 00:13:31,960
Gentlemen, we currently have 133 specified slot cards of 90 different types.

204
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:35,500
And of course, it's all thanks to your tireless efforts.

205
00:13:36,220 --> 00:13:40,020
Of the remaining 10 cards, we know the location of 7 of them.

206
00:13:40,840 --> 00:13:42,440
They'll be ours before you know it.

207
00:13:43,680 --> 00:13:46,580
But, Tescara's group is closing in.

208
00:13:47,240 --> 00:13:50,060
They've obtained the same number of specified slot cards.

209
00:13:50,580 --> 00:13:54,800
And now, the final hurdle will likely be a showdown against their group.

210
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:59,960
However, I believe we have more spell cards, and of much higher quality.

211
00:14:00,560 --> 00:14:03,680
So, our victory is all but assured!

212
00:14:06,180 --> 00:14:07,100
May I?

213
00:14:07,360 --> 00:14:08,700
