217
00:14:27,020 --> 00:14:27,620
What?

218
00:14:27,800 --> 00:14:28,720
The bomber?

219
00:14:29,680 --> 00:14:30,760
Hey, wait.

220
00:14:31,100 --> 00:14:32,280
What are you talking about?

221
00:14:32,420 --> 00:14:33,840
Please, hear me out.

222
00:14:34,400 --> 00:14:37,660
I've already planted bombs on each and every one of you.

223
00:14:38,760 --> 00:14:39,760
You what?

224
00:14:39,880 --> 00:14:41,520
How did you even do that?

225
00:14:41,700 --> 00:14:43,020
Yeah, you're kidding, right?

226
00:14:43,020 --> 00:14:45,400
Calm down and listen.

227
00:14:49,720 --> 00:14:54,900
Oh, dear.

228
00:14:55,380 --> 00:14:58,600
You've disrupted the proper sequence of my explanation.

229
00:14:59,540 --> 00:15:00,840
This is my ability.

230
00:15:01,620 --> 00:15:02,540
Little flower.

231
00:15:03,880 --> 00:15:07,300
You see, I can blow up anything that I grab.

232
00:15:07,760 --> 00:15:09,840
But, it isn't all that strong.

233
00:15:10,620 --> 00:15:12,400
He's still alive, of course.

234
00:15:12,400 --> 00:15:19,420
However, if the bombs on your bodies were to suddenly explode, you would die.

235
00:15:19,420 --> 00:15:23,500
A bomb!

236
00:15:23,740 --> 00:15:24,700
But where is it?

237
00:15:25,400 --> 00:15:26,160
Listen up.

238
00:15:26,720 --> 00:15:29,580
And I'll be more than happy to tell you how to disarm them.

239
00:15:30,640 --> 00:15:32,580
Let's begin with how I set them.

240
00:15:33,340 --> 00:15:36,900
That was simply by touching the place on the target I wished to explode.

241
00:15:37,480 --> 00:15:39,560
And uttering a certain key word.

242
00:15:40,120 --> 00:15:41,420
Which is...

243
00:15:41,420 --> 00:15:43,700
Bomber.

244
00:15:43,700 --> 00:15:43,760
Bomber.

245
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:50,480
It sounds like it was the Bomber.

246
00:15:52,480 --> 00:15:53,080
Listen.

247
00:15:53,780 --> 00:15:55,020
Beware of the Bomber.

248
00:15:55,020 --> 00:16:01,460
To disarm the bombs, you must touch me somewhere on my body and then say the phrase,

249
00:16:01,580 --> 00:16:02,620
I caught the bomber.

250
00:16:03,020 --> 00:16:05,840
That said, don't forget about my secret weapon.

251
00:16:06,360 --> 00:16:07,740
The little flower ability.

252
00:16:08,320 --> 00:16:11,340
I can use it to stop anyone who tries to touch me.

253
00:16:12,340 --> 00:16:15,580
You must be very careful when attempting to disarm the bombs.

254
00:16:16,120 --> 00:16:16,880
That's all.

255
00:16:16,880 --> 00:16:26,740
What's the matter now?

256
00:16:27,340 --> 00:16:29,900
My other ability is countdown.

257
00:16:32,560 --> 00:16:35,500
Why am I telling you all of this, you might be wondering?

258
00:16:36,700 --> 00:16:40,140
That's the condition for arming the bombs I planted on you.

259
00:16:40,820 --> 00:16:41,320
Then you.

260
00:16:41,800 --> 00:16:45,440
We're just waiting for the day that all of the karts and members were gathered.

261
00:16:45,440 --> 00:16:48,080
And now, I have a proposition.

262
00:16:48,920 --> 00:16:53,400
I will trade your lives for the 90 specified slot cards you've obtained.

263
00:16:54,360 --> 00:17:01,780
If you agree to my terms, then I will use an alternative method to simultaneously disarm all of the bombs.

264
00:17:02,860 --> 00:17:06,940
Do nothing, and all of you will die when the counter reaches zero.

265
00:17:07,860 --> 00:17:10,020
You should discuss this amongst yourselves.

266
00:17:11,220 --> 00:17:14,160
I'll be waiting for you at Mr. Patera's old mansion.

267
00:17:14,160 --> 00:17:17,640
And whoever comes must come alone.

268
00:17:18,480 --> 00:17:20,520
Do you have a screw loose or something, buddy?

269
00:17:20,860 --> 00:17:25,240
If we just catch you right here and now and disarm the bombs, it's all over.

270
00:17:25,620 --> 00:17:26,740
It's you against us.

271
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:28,840
Do you really think we'll just let you walk away?

272
00:17:29,700 --> 00:17:30,180
Relax.

273
00:17:30,580 --> 00:17:33,180
If you get too excited, the countdown will accelerate.

274
00:17:33,980 --> 00:17:37,480
I should have mentioned that the counter is linked to your heartbeat.

275
00:17:37,900 --> 00:17:38,220
What?

276
00:17:39,760 --> 00:17:40,300
Hook.

277
00:17:40,300 --> 00:17:40,360
Hook.

278
00:17:41,860 --> 00:17:42,380
No!

279
00:17:45,260 --> 00:17:47,660
I do hope that we meet again soon.

280
00:17:48,200 --> 00:17:48,600
Leave!

281
00:17:48,700 --> 00:17:49,100
On!

282
00:17:51,100 --> 00:17:52,920
He escaped out of the game!

283
00:17:53,320 --> 00:17:53,640
Hurry!

284
00:17:53,740 --> 00:17:54,760
We gotta follow him!

285
00:17:55,240 --> 00:17:55,580
Wait.

286
00:17:55,900 --> 00:17:59,100
But if we leave, the spell cards in our binders will vanish!

287
00:17:59,320 --> 00:18:00,320
So what do we do?

288
00:18:00,800 --> 00:18:01,940
Just calm down!

289
00:18:02,500 --> 00:18:04,140
Going after that guy would be foolish!

290
00:18:04,140 --> 00:18:08,000
Did you already forget why we decided to team up in the first place?

291
00:18:08,220 --> 00:18:10,400
Because none of us are strong enough fighters!

292
00:18:11,100 --> 00:18:14,480
Does anyone here actually think we're powerful enough to beat him?

293
00:18:15,240 --> 00:18:16,180
It's impossible.

294
00:18:17,180 --> 00:18:18,800
He must be quite strong.

295
00:18:19,220 --> 00:18:20,840
His nin abilities prove it.

296
00:18:21,520 --> 00:18:27,980
If all of us decided to attack him together as a unified front, he could simply use Little Flower to stop us.

297
00:18:27,980 --> 00:18:28,900
Damn!

298
00:18:29,280 --> 00:18:31,100
We were getting so close, too!

299
00:18:31,720 --> 00:18:34,620
To start, it's imperative that we come to a consensus.

300
00:18:35,340 --> 00:18:38,340
Do we try to fight, or do we just hand over the cards?

301
00:18:38,780 --> 00:18:39,540
Hand them over.

302
00:18:40,120 --> 00:18:40,540
Please.

303
00:18:41,460 --> 00:18:42,200
Do it.

304
00:18:44,680 --> 00:18:47,880
I'm sorry, but Jispa is running out of time.

305
00:18:47,880 --> 00:18:56,120
What a surprise.

306
00:18:56,760 --> 00:18:59,580
I had assumed that Nyx would be the one to show up.

307
00:19:00,040 --> 00:19:01,100
I'm surprised, too.

308
00:19:01,460 --> 00:19:02,620
Thought Judah had company.

309
00:19:04,980 --> 00:19:06,140
Sub and Bara.

310
00:19:06,540 --> 00:19:07,760
They're the other bombers.

311
00:19:08,640 --> 00:19:11,240
Now, I'll have to ask you to hand over your ring.

312
00:19:13,100 --> 00:19:13,920
What's wrong?

313
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:16,800
I can't turn it over yet.

314
00:19:17,640 --> 00:19:19,840
Thing is, we still haven't agreed.

315
00:19:20,480 --> 00:19:21,740
And Nyx has a request.

316
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:26,520
He wants you to let us have the Angel's Breath card so that we can use it to save Jispa.

317
00:19:26,680 --> 00:19:27,660
I refuse!

318
00:19:27,940 --> 00:19:30,020
As it stands, neither side can win!

319
00:19:30,080 --> 00:19:30,300
Huh?

320
00:19:30,920 --> 00:19:34,140
You don't realize how hysterical they're all being right now.

321
00:19:34,300 --> 00:19:37,840
If they can't decide in time and they explode, then you lose everything.

322
00:19:38,200 --> 00:19:39,740
All the data in their rings.

323
00:19:40,340 --> 00:19:41,440
You need me.

324
00:19:41,440 --> 00:19:42,720
You can convince them.

325
00:19:43,140 --> 00:19:44,280
Is that what you're saying?

326
00:19:44,280 --> 00:19:48,120
Are you really trying to bargain with me?

327
00:19:48,120 --> 00:19:56,460
Because when you sit down to negotiate, you have to demonstrate to your opponent just how calm and insane you are.

328
00:19:56,860 --> 00:19:57,840
Hey, wait!

329
00:19:58,040 --> 00:19:59,840
If you kill me now...

330
00:19:59,840 --> 00:20:03,800
Don't worry.

331
00:20:03,800 --> 00:20:11,000
If you kill a player outside the game and take their ring, their specified slots card data remains intact.

332
00:20:12,000 --> 00:20:16,320
Well, someone has the cards, but I highly doubt that it's you.

333
00:20:16,320 --> 00:20:29,440
I brought you a gift.

334
00:20:29,440 --> 00:20:35,320
You won't get another chance.

335
00:20:35,600 --> 00:20:36,020
Got it?

336
00:20:36,980 --> 00:20:37,500
Leave.

337
00:20:38,500 --> 00:20:41,240
Hand over the leave card right now.

338
00:20:41,720 --> 00:20:43,620
I need to go, so hurry.

339
00:20:43,960 --> 00:20:44,800
You're crazy!

340
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:48,500
Leave is a really valuable card, and we can't waste any!

341
00:20:48,820 --> 00:20:50,480
All right, have it your way.

342
00:20:50,860 --> 00:20:55,520
But if I don't come back here, you can't disarm all of your bombs simultaneously.

343
00:20:55,880 --> 00:20:56,280
What?

344
00:20:56,280 --> 00:21:00,120
Well, I'm also a bomber, so...

345
00:21:00,120 --> 00:21:02,540
There are three of us.

346
00:21:03,020 --> 00:21:04,960
Well, Genthrou's the main one.

347
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:07,500
The rest of us are basically his wingmen.

348
00:21:08,620 --> 00:21:13,780
When the three of us join our right thumbs and say the key word, the bombs will be destroyed.

349
00:21:14,800 --> 00:21:17,100
And that is the alternative method.

350
00:21:18,360 --> 00:21:18,820
Whatever.

351
00:21:19,300 --> 00:21:23,800
I'll take my time returning by traditional means, and you'll all be dead soon.

352
00:21:23,800 --> 00:21:26,200
Wait! Hold on a minute!

353
00:21:28,100 --> 00:21:29,920
Here, you can just take it.

354
00:21:33,280 --> 00:21:35,260
Should have done that in the first place!

355
00:21:36,360 --> 00:21:40,220
We'll need leave cards when the deal is made, so get three of them ready.

356
00:21:40,500 --> 00:21:40,980
Got that?

357
00:21:40,980 --> 00:21:41,900
Let's go!

358
00:21:41,980 --> 00:21:42,680
Let's go!

359
00:21:43,300 --> 00:21:43,800
Let's go!

360
00:21:46,860 --> 00:21:57,620
A mere 12 hours earlier, Genthrou revealed himself as the infamous bomber, and a single boat attempted to invade the island from the outside.

361
00:21:57,620 --> 00:22:06,720
So it does exist in the real world. This must be it Greed Island

362
00:22:27,620 --> 00:22:42,620
Come share your明日を目指す 朝日に照らされた傷 笑い合って 終わることない旅を続けよう

363
00:22:43,620 --> 00:22:51,620
向かい風としていながら それでも進む理由がある

364
00:22:51,620 --> 00:22:58,620
だから友よ 置いてくためだけに生きるのはまだ 早いだろ

365
00:22:58,620 --> 00:23:06,620
身につけたもの 抱え込んだもの 手放したとき 始まる何か

366
00:23:06,620 --> 00:23:17,620
上手く生きてく レシピを破り捨てて感じるリズム そう僕らのやり方で

367
00:23:17,620 --> 00:23:21,620
次の動画でお会いしましょう!

